<Project>

  <!--
    Ship only the Whisper natives the target platform can load.

    Whisper.net.Runtime hands its desktop binaries to MSBuild as <None> items
    conditioned on the *target framework* alone. We target plain `net10.0`, so
    every one of its conditions matches and a `-r win-x64` publish collects all
    of them: Linux .so files, macOS .dylib files, an Apple Metal shader, and
    arm64 and x86 builds. None of them can ever be loaded, and together they are
    about 15 MB — roughly 8% of a self-contained build, carried by every user on
    both platforms.

    RID filtering normally handles this, but only for natives laid out as
    `runtimes/<rid>/native/`. These arrive as ordinary content with a TargetPath,
    so nothing filters them and they are simply copied.

    Filtered here at the publish list rather than at the <None> items, because
    the package is referenced by Core while the files are shipped by App: by the
    time they matter they have already crossed a project boundary, and
    ResolvedFileToPublish is the one list that sees them whatever route they
    took. It is also the list that decides what actually lands in an archive,
    which is the thing we mean to change.

    The path is matched with forward slashes because that is how the package
    itself spells its TargetPath, on every platform. If that ever changed, the
    win-x64 files would stop matching and be dropped along with the rest — a
    publish missing the natives it needs, rather than a quiet regression.

    Scoped by source package rather than by anything shaped like a native, so it
    cannot quietly discard another dependency's files. With no RID there is
    nothing to filter against and everything stays.
  -->
  <Target Name="DropWhisperNativesForOtherPlatforms"
          AfterTargets="ComputeResolvedFilesToPublishList"
          Condition="'$(RuntimeIdentifier)' != ''">

    <ItemGroup>
      <_ForeignWhisperNative
        Include="@(ResolvedFileToPublish)"
        Condition="$([System.String]::new('%(ResolvedFileToPublish.Identity)').ToLowerInvariant().Contains('whisper.net.runtime'))
                   and !$([System.String]::new('%(ResolvedFileToPublish.RelativePath)').StartsWith('runtimes/$(RuntimeIdentifier)/'))" />

      <ResolvedFileToPublish Remove="@(_ForeignWhisperNative)" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <Message Importance="normal"
             Text="Whisper natives dropped as unloadable on $(RuntimeIdentifier): @(_ForeignWhisperNative->Count())" />
  </Target>

</Project>
